sentences.text:
In the event of arrest of the applicant, involved in the above noted case or on his surrender before the trial court within 15 days from today i.e. on or before 06.05..2023, whichever is earlier, he shall be released on anticipatory bail on his furnishing a personal bond of Rs. 50,000/- with two sureties in the like amount to the satisfaction of the Trial Court or Station House Officer of the Police Station concerned/ Investigating Officer as the case may be subject to the following conditions:
i. The applicant shall make himself available for interrogation by a police officer, as and when required;
ii.

The applicant shall not directly or indirectly, make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade them from disclosing such facts to the Court or to any police officer;
Vijay Kumar Alias Vijay Kumar Yadav vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Home Lko. ... on 21 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/150430925/
